from plan_content import week

week('Prepare technical quotation packages','Procurement','procurement',
 'G2 quotation baseline, ten-joint duty summaries, interfaces and written spending policy.',
 'A quote request is not a purchase. Compare complete assemblies with driver, transmission, mounts, freight, taxes and spares.',
 [9,15,44],['G2'],[],'''
Create the actuator RFQ template || Build a request-for-information table for continuous torque-speed, peak duration/recovery, thermal duty, efficiency, bearings, backdrive/brake and power/regen behavior. || Add exact joint interfaces, quantity, driver option, firmware, communication, lead time and landed-price fields; attach only the accepted quotation revision. || Each of ten joints has a required envelope and every unknown vendor field is explicitly unanswered. || actuator_RFQ_template.md
Prepare the structural fabrication RFQ || Package accepted concept/interface drawings, material candidates, critical tolerances, inspection needs and unresolved design-review conditions for a qualified shop. || Ask for separate fabrication, setup, inspection, material and delivery costs; no instruction to fabricate is included. || The package says quotation only and identifies which drawings still need fabrication release. || fabrication_RFQ_template.md
Prepare the support and rigging RFQ || Request an engineered robot-arrest/support solution or documented rental/access arrangement from a qualified provider. || Include projected mass, geometry, site survey and load-path questions; request design, installation, inspection and access terms as separate costs. || No assumed anchor rating or human harness is specified as an accepted robot solution. || robot_support_RFQ_template.md
Prepare power and safety sourcing questions || Request exact pack/charger compatibility, protection, full-charge voltage, fault/regen behavior and reviewed safety-component interfaces. || Keep the qualified electrical/controls reviewers responsible for ratings and architecture suitability; document vendor exclusions. || The requests ask for technical evidence and do not treat a component purchase as whole-system safety certification. || power_safety_RFQ_template.md
Prepare feet sensors and handling questions || Request sensor ranges/calibration, sole material data, supported module/counterbalance options and captured-payload retention components. || Attach the 2 kg stationary task and candidate reach as analysis requirements, with no 5 kg or cargo-walking promise. || Every requested component links to a Year 1 requirement and a planned inspection/test. || feet_handling_RFQ_template.md
Request and organize actual quotations || Review the packages with Faisal, then personally send quotation requests through your chosen channels; this website sends nothing automatically. || Save actual replies and dates, including incomplete responses; record currency, validity, quantities, configuration and delivery assumptions. || Every quoted price is distinguishable from an allowance and no order or payment has been made. || quotation_response_register.csv
Review quotation completeness || Compare received technical data to each requirement and mark compliant, noncompliant or unanswered with source references. || Follow up on the highest-impact missing fields and retain alternative candidates without selecting from price or peak torque alone. || No candidate is marked qualified while continuous/thermal/interface evidence is missing. || quotation_completeness_review.md
''')
week('Reconcile the BOM and procurement gate','Procurement','budget',
 'Actual vendor quotations, technical comparison, G2 baseline and current mass/cost records.',
 'Committed spend + remaining landed costs + spares/reserve must stay <=USD 10000. Do not count a donation until documented.',
 [3,4,9,15,44],['G2'],[],'''
Build the landed cost BOM || Enter exact part, revision, quantity, unit price, driver/accessory inclusion, freight, tax/duty and quote validity for each required line. || Include fall protection, fixtures, instruments, independent review, fabrication, panels, software and reserve; flag unquoted totals. || The total includes all required cash costs and no missing input silently becomes zero. || landed_cost_BOM.csv
Compare technical compliance by joint || For every lower-body joint, trace required torque-speed/duty to the chosen candidate's supported continuous and peak envelope. || Document thermal, bearing, brake/backdrive, power and interface suitability or an explicit deviation needing review. || Ten joint rows have evidence-based dispositions; a peak-only match remains unqualified. || joint_candidate_qualification.csv
Reconcile the revised mass estimate || Replace candidate mass allowances with vendor and CAD figures for the same BOM configuration; include all mounts, battery and shell. || Compare against 55 kg target and >65 kg review threshold, showing residual reserve or overrun numerically. || No selected part is counted in cost but omitted from onboard mass. || procurement_mass_reconciliation.csv
Resolve the budget route with Faisal || Present the actual total and gaps plus documented reuse/sponsorship or redesign options; retain the current cap unless explicitly revised. || If the route exceeds funding, record procurement BLOCKED and define a specific engineering rework package instead of cutting safety controls. || A feasible funding claim requires a fully covered, technically credible BOM with written evidence. || D01_funding_disposition_update.md
Assemble the G3 procurement packet || Include accepted requirements, frozen architecture, mass, duty, thermal/power calculations, simulation, vendor data, interfaces, budget and inspection plan. || Name the independent reviewer and authorized fabricator; list the exact proposed order lines, amounts and release scope. || All G3 prerequisites are present or clearly listed as blockers; no blanket purchasing authority is requested. || G3_procurement_review_packet.md
Hold the independent procurement review || Ask the qualified reviewer and Faisal to inspect technical suitability, cash reconciliation and remaining deviations. || Record actual approval, rework or blocked disposition for the exact revision; populate the website gate record only from that evidence. || G3 is not released merely because a target budget spreadsheet adds to 10000 USD. || G3_procurement_disposition.md
Place only specifically authorized orders || If G3 and owner spending authorization are real and current, order only the released BOM lines and retain receipts and promised delivery dates. || If blocked, spend the session updating alternative candidates and the precise missing-evidence list without ordering anything. || Every commitment has an approval reference, exact configuration and amount; blocked work has no new expenditure. || authorized_order_register.csv
''')
